/*
  core/masks/compare_behavior.spthy -- f_H for the COMPARE action class, CEREMONY-AGNOSTIC (AGNOSTIC_MASKS.md).
  Collapses the old *_verify (read !VerifyReq, wrote !KeyChecked, emitted Accept) and *_verify_op (read
  !Op 'verify', wrote VerifyDone) masks. The ceremony reports only OBSERVABLES in
  !StepData(P,vid,<offered,reference>) -- the artifact the UI displays and the trusted reference an
  attentive check would consult (keyserver entry, session fingerprint). The VERDICT is derived HERE,
  in the response layer: the Attentive rule PERFORMS the comparison (matches offered = reference), it
  does not read a producer-declared 'genuine'/'tampered' oracle tag. The response manifests as a
  generic Checked(P,vid) that a thin per-ceremony adapter wraps (!KeyChecked / VerifyDone).

    Attentive ('discerning') fires only when offered = reference (the pattern <k,k>) -> on a
      substituted artifact NO rule fires (the verification stalls -- the attentive user rejects).
      Preserves P3_attentive_never_accepts_tampered because a substituted artifact cannot equal the
      unforgeable reference; and if an adversary re-offers the GENUINE artifact, acceptance is correct.
    Naive ('credulous') accepts ANY artifact without looking at !StepData at all -> a Norman MISTAKE
      (confident wrong action from no mental model); Accept(vid) is emitted so a VerifyShutout
      mitigation (Accept on a Tampered vid forbidden) can block the harmful case. Tampered(vid)
      remains the PRODUCER's provenance marker -- lemma vocabulary, never read by a response rule.

  RespMask(P,mask) is gated by mask_state.spthy exactly as before. Action facts (Verify/Accept/Mistake/
  Answered) are unchanged, so the lemmas are untouched.
*/

// Attentive: performs the comparison -- fires only when the offered artifact equals the reference.
rule Compare_attentive [color=#27ae60]:
    [ !Step(P, vid, 'compare'), !StepData(P, vid, <k, k>), !OutcomePolicy(mask, 'compare', 'discerning') ]
  --[ Verify(P, vid, mask), RespMask(P, mask), Accept(P, vid), Answered(vid) ]->
    [ Checked(P, vid) ]

// Naive: accepts ANY artifact -> a Mistake (harmful iff the producer marked the vid Tampered).
rule Compare_naive [color=#27ae60]:
    [ !Step(P, vid, 'compare'), !OutcomePolicy(mask, 'compare', 'credulous') ]
  --[ Verify(P, vid, mask), RespMask(P, mask), Mask(P,'Attentive',mask), Mistake(P, vid), Accept(P, vid), Answered(vid) ]->
    [ Checked(P, vid) ]
